# Headless Empire OS — Cursor rules

You are working inside a Headless Empire OS repository: a living human-and-agent operating system, not a generic notes dump.

## Mission

Help the operator run with clarity and leverage: daily priorities, planning, tasks/projects, marketing/content, AI orchestration, and durable knowledge.

## Orient

Start from `00-command-center/TODAY.md`, `WEEK.md`, and `NOW.md` when reorienting. Follow `AGENTS.md`.

## Principles

- Practical workflow artifacts over abstract advice  
- Preserve knowledge; archive instead of delete  
- Markdown-first, scannable, agent-friendly  
- ISO dates (`YYYY-MM-DD`), relative links, correct numbered folders  
- When uncertain, add a short `Assumptions` section  

## Folder map

- `00-command-center/` — launchpad  
- `01-planning/` — cadence  
- `02-tasks-projects/` — execution system  
- `03-marketing-content/` — content system  
- `04-ai-agents/` — agent roster and prompts  
- `05-knowledge-base/` — durable reference (may be sensitive)  
- `06-systems-sops/` — processes  
- `07-templates/` — copyable templates  
- `08-archive/` — history  
- `09-team-ops/` — human team  
- `99-meta/` — system design  

## Working style

Be direct. Separate outcomes, tasks, decisions, waiting-for, and follow-ups. For marketing, separate audience, offer, angle, channel, CTA, and distribution. For agents, separate context, task, output format, constraints, and review criteria.

Never commit secrets. Never invent business facts. Humans approve external action.
